cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Völva, please cite it and name the version you used."
title: "Völva: crystallite size and microstrain from powder X-ray diffraction line broadening"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Reeves-McLaren
    given-names: Nik
    affiliation: University of Sheffield
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1061-1230"
version: 4.1.2
abstract: >-
  Völva measures crystallite size and microstrain from powder X-ray
  diffraction line broadening. It fits each reflection as a pseudo-Voigt
  Kα1 + Kα2 doublet, removes a measured instrument profile component by
  component (Gaussian widths in quadrature, Lorentzian widths linearly),
  runs six methods (Scherrer, single-line Voigt, Monshi-Scherrer,
  Williamson-Hall, Voigt Williamson-Hall and Halder-Wagner) with Monte Carlo
  uncertainties, and reports where they agree, which assumptions fail, and
  when a size is only a bound. It is a PySide6 desktop application, a
  command line and a Python package.
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/SuperBladesman/Volva"
keywords:
  - X-ray diffraction
  - powder diffraction
  - crystallite size
  - microstrain
  - line profile analysis
  - Scherrer
  - Williamson-Hall
  - Halder-Wagner
